[48.642013, "i", "cat << 'EOF' >> trace_intrusion.py\n\n# Let's map GUID to Image\nguid_to_img = {}\nfor e in events:\n    guid = (e['process_guid'] or '').lower()\n    img = e['image']\n    if guid in guids and img:\n        guid_to_img[guid] = img\n\nprint(\"GUID mapping:\", json.dumps(guid_to_img, indent=2))\n\n# Let's find ALL events that are related to these GUIDs\n# 1. Any event where process_guid or parent_process_guid is in guids.\n# 2. Any event where the message/details contain one of these GUIDs.\n# 3. Any security log event that corresponds to these processes. How do we find these?\n# Security log processes are often matched by ProcessId (hex or dec) or ProcessName/Image, but also timestamp and activity.\n# Specifically, let's look at Security Process Creation (4688) which corresponds to Sysmon (1).\n# Sysmon (1) and Security (4688) always occur in pairs for the same process start.\n# Let's look at the correlation between them.\n\nEOF\npython3 trace_intrusion.py\n"]
